ALREADY has and that the R-87 build must not destroy. They pass now because
there is no telemetry at all; they must still pass once there is.

  TEL-SRC-06  connect-src carries no new host.
              Passes because the CSP is untouched. Fails the moment an
              implementer reaches for a hosted analytics script instead of the
              same-origin Cloud Function.

  TEL-SRC-14  No consent wall, banner or preference dialog.
              Passes because nothing is collected. R-87 forbids ever adding one,
              so this must survive the build.

  TEL-SRC-17  No third-party analytics package is a dependency.
              Same shape: a guard against the easy wrong answer.

  TEL-183     The BIDIRECTIONAL self-claim lock. Passes today in its "both old"
              branch: no instrumentation exists AND the legacy claim
              "no analytics, no trackers, no cookies" is still on the page, which
              is honest. It flips to FAIL the instant lib/telemetry/beacon.ts or
              exports.telemetryCollect appears without the two published
